## User story

As a platform security stakeholder,
I want dedicated IPP (payload-processing) pods per AITenant with isolated networking and gateway wiring,
So that request payloads, provider credentials, and ext_proc state are not shared across tenants in a multi-tenant cluster.

## Description

Today MaaS deploys a **single shared** IPP fleet in the gateway namespace (`payload-processing`, `payload-pre-processing`, one `EnvoyFilter`). All tenant reconciles SSA-apply the same object names; the last reconcile wins on `EnvoyFilter.spec.targetRefs`. Shared IPP pods also hold cluster-scoped RBAC (`payload-processing-reader` ClusterRole) with cluster-wide Secret list/watch and process inference traffic for every gateway.

Leadership direction: mirror the existing **per-tenant maas-api** pattern — one IPP stack per AITenant, each wired to that tenant's Gateway, with teardown on AITenant delete.

### Scope (this ticket)

**`models-as-a-service` — tenant platform reconcile**

- Per-tenant resource names in `openshift-ingress` (default tenant keeps legacy unsuffixed names):
  - Deployments: `payload-processing[-{tenant}]`, `payload-pre-processing[-{tenant}]`
  - Services, DestinationRules, EnvoyFilter, ServiceAccount, plugins ConfigMap, NetworkPolicy, ClusterRoleBinding
- Unique Deployment/Service selectors via `maas.opendatahub.io/tenant-instance` (required when multiple IPP stacks share the gateway namespace)
- Patch `GATEWAY_NAME`, `GATEWAY_NAMESPACE`, and `TENANT_NAMESPACE` on the main IPP Deployment
- EnvoyFilter `targetRef` + grpc clusters + WasmPlugin anchor per tenant gateway
- NetworkPolicy: ext_proc ingress only from **that tenant's** gateway pods (`gateway.networking.k8s.io/gateway-name`)
- Delete IPP gateway resources in `cleanupTenantResources` on MaasTenantConfig removal

### Follow-up (separate ticket — IPP binary)

- Namespace-scoped Role replacing ClusterRole Secret access
- Controller/informer watch scope limited to `TENANT_NAMESPACE`
- Secret cache namespace filter in `apikey-injection` (defense in depth)

## Operator changes

No ODH operator subscription or DSC changes. Deployed via existing MaaS tenant reconcile (MaasTenantConfig / AITenant bootstrap). Customization affects gateway-namespace operands reconciled by maas-controller.

## Acceptance criteria

Given an AITenant with a dedicated Gateway (not the default tenant),
 When MaasTenantConfig reconciles platform resources,
 Then Deployments `payload-processing-{tenant}` and `payload-pre-processing-{tenant}`, matching Services, DestinationRules, EnvoyFilter `payload-processing-{tenant}`, and NetworkPolicy exist in the gateway namespace with tenant tracking labels.

Given a per-tenant IPP Deployment,
 When the pod starts,
 Then it has `GATEWAY_NAME` and `GATEWAY_NAMESPACE` set to that AITenant's gateway and `TENANT_NAMESPACE` set to the tenant admin namespace.

Given tenant A and tenant B both reconcile,
 When each tenant's EnvoyFilter is applied,
 Then each EnvoyFilter `spec.targetRefs[0].name` matches that tenant's gateway and grpc clusters reference that tenant's IPP Services (no last-reconcile overwrite of a single shared EnvoyFilter).

**Given per-tenant IPP NetworkPolicies in the gateway namespace (`openshift-ingress`), when ext_proc traffic arrives, then ingress is allowed only from gateway pods labeled with that tenant's `gateway.networking.k8s.io/gateway-name`, not from other tenants' gateway pods.**

Given Kustomize changes to per-tenant IPP base manifests and tenant reconcile patches,
 When `kustomize build maas-api/deploy/overlays/odh | kubectl apply --dry-run=client` is run after rendering for a non-default tenant,
 Then suffixed IPP resource names and EnvoyFilter grpc cluster names are present.

Given an AITenant-managed MaasTenantConfig is deleted,
 When `cleanupTenantResources` runs,
 Then per-tenant IPP Deployments, Services, DestinationRules, EnvoyFilter, NetworkPolicy, ServiceAccount, plugins ConfigMap, and ClusterRoleBinding are removed from the gateway namespace.

Given the default tenant (`models-as-a-service`, empty tenant identifier),
 When platform resources reconcile,
 Then legacy unsuffixed names (`payload-processing`, etc.) are preserved for backward compatibility.

## Testability

- `go test ./maas-controller/pkg/platform/tenantreconcile/...` — unit tests for default and non-default tenant overlay rendering (resource names, env vars, EnvoyFilter clusters, NetworkPolicy selectors).
- Manual multi-tenant cluster: create two AITenants; verify distinct IPP Deployments, distinct EnvoyFilter targetRefs, hybrid BBR on both gateways simultaneously.
- Verify tenant delete removes suffixed IPP resources without affecting the default tenant stack.

## Documentation

- Update `docs/content/concepts/multi-tenancy.md` — add per-tenant IPP to the isolation model (API + gateway + IPP).
